{"title":"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems\">2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) #1</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems\">2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) #2</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In 1998, the population of Canada was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/4/f6474c5e43108a7ec87f8589209a4226b6fbb8d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30.3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" /> million. Which number is the same as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/4/f6474c5e43108a7ec87f8589209a4226b6fbb8d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30.3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" /> million.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/3/b73bd5f3043f48325ea16a5b326ebe3121fcbf49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 30~300~000 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 303~000~000 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 30~000 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 303~000 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 30~300~000~000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"747\" height=\"18\" />  \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can simply convert <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/4/f6474c5e43108a7ec87f8589209a4226b6fbb8d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30.3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" /> million into a number. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/4/f6474c5e43108a7ec87f8589209a4226b6fbb8d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30.3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" /> million is the same as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/7/c470640f75ea620e344ccbbf7633958a881d4980.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30.3 \\times 10^{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"82\" height=\"18\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/6/ad68a6a4b14c6b6de753c425e3be1d17736390cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(A) } 30~300~000}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"133\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Problem</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(G